  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **Browser:** the **Setups** row under Setup is drawn whenever the Setup section is open, not only once `setup::names` is non-empty (`panes::browser_rows`). The page already handles the no-setup case (\"No setups in this document ... Create first setup\").\n- **Ribbon:** the Setup group is now `[Setups, Stock, Origin, Tools, Machine]`. The new `Cmd::Setups` cell targets `UiTarget::Setups` through `actions::target`, with the tip \"Setups: create, activate and delete the document's setups\".\n- **Icon:** both the cell and the browser row use the existing workholding glyph (`Icon::Fixture`, `assets/ui/fixture.png`). This adds no asset and changes nothing in `LICENSES.md`. The browser row used to show the work-offset glyph; it now matches the ribbon cell, and the Setups cell no longer looks the same as Origin next to it.\n- **Command path unchanged:** **Create first setup** still queues `CommandKind::CreateSetup`, which runs the app's `CreateSetup` through the history, so undo works.\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/322-first-setup.md`.\n\n## Readings / how tested\n\n- New kittest test `egui_app::tests::first_setup::a_fresh_document_reaches_setups_and_creates_the_first_one_undoably`, on a blank shell with no seed:\n  - the Setups browser row is present;\n  - a real pointer click on the ribbon's Setups cell sets `UiTarget::Setups`;\n  - clicking **Create first setup** makes exactly one setup, and the history can undo it;\n  - undo removes the setup and the page returns to its no-setup state.\n- Updated `setup_navigation_is_always_reachable_and_operations_keep_a_flat_browser` (renamed from `..._is_conditional_...`): the blank document now shows the Setups leaf, and the Setup group now lists the Setups cell. `tips_match_the_imgui_table` has a row for the new tip.\n- Shell snapshots regenerated with `UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1` from `crates/ui`: `egui_app.png`, `egui_app_light.png` and `egui_tool_editor.png`. I compared each against the old golden. The only differences are the new Setups cell (the bar re-spaces to fit it) and the new Setups row (the rows below it move down one).\n- Quick gate, all from CWD `crates/ui`:\n  - camcraft-ui lib: 283 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored;\n  - `--test egui_app`: 3 passed;\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not exercised: the live GUI (not launched, per policy), and app suites (no app code touched).\n\nNote: `panes.rs` and `tests.rs` were already past the 400-line limit before this PR. This PR adds about 10 lines to `panes.rs`, and the new test goes in its own file.\n\nChangelog: A new document can open the Setups page from the browser's Setups row and a new Setups ribbon cell, so its first setup can be created (undoable)\n\nFixes #322\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
